    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0287" n="273" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EAC/8–1644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-08-16T23:00:00-04:00">August 16, 1944—11
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6506. Your 6591, August 16, 1 p.m., our 6366 August 11. Chiang Kai-shek having
                    authorized Dr. H. H. Kung<anchor n="22" xml:id="d147-f1"/> and General Shang
                        Chen<anchor n="23" xml:id="d147-f2"/> now in Washington to be informed of
                    the proposed terms for the unconditional surrender of Germany as approved by the
                    European Advisory Commission, the terms were read to these officials on August
                    14. We impressed upon the Chinese officials the top secrecy of the document and
                    asked their assurances that the terms would not be communicated to Chungking by
                    mail or by cable. The Chinese officials gave these assurances. No document was
                    handed to the Chinese officials.<anchor n="24" xml:id="d147-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d147-f1" n="22" xml:id="d147-f1-content">
                <p>Chinese Minister of Finance and Chief Delegate to the United Nations Monetary and
                    Financial Conference at Bretton Woods.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f2" n="23" xml:id="d147-f2-content">
                <p>Head of the Chinese Military Mission in the United States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d147-f3" n="24" xml:id="d147-f3-content">
                <p>A memorandum by President Roosevelt to the Secretary of State, dated August 21,
                    stated: “I do not think it is necessary to press this matter in view of the
                    feeling of Gousev.” (740.00119 EAC/8–2144)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
